# Security headers for every page (Cloudflare Pages reads this file from the build output).
# Kept compatible with migrated WordPress content: the site may still embed YouTube, donation
# forms, maps and so on; these rules only stop other sites framing this one, force HTTPS, and
# switch off browser features the site doesn't use. A stricter Content Security Policy (limiting
# scripts and frames to named sites) would need a list per client, so it isn't set here.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), browsing-topics=()
